  "id": "6eea44de-52dd-42f5-add7-eb4cea014d4d",
  "title": "Unified 3D Gaussian Splatting and Ray Tracing for Realistic Scene Reconstruction",
  "summary": "RealityBridge combines multimodal controls and lightweight GateNet to enhance 3DGS driving simulations, while the 4D radar-camera framework improves full-scene perception. Both methods address the need for efficient, accurate 3D reconstruction in autonomous driving and medical imaging. VoroTracing and 3DGART demonstrate advancements in real-time rendering using differentiable ray tracing, achieving higher throughput and better performance than prior methods.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RealityBridge and the 4D radar-camera framework both address the need for efficient, accurate 3D reconstruction in autonomous driving and medical imaging.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "3DGART achieves a 3-3.5× speedup over per-pixel baseline and 4× over 3DGRT on Mip-NeRF 360, while improving quality.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both 3D Gaussian Splatting and ray-based rendering techniques are designed to handle view-dependent ordering and secondary effects such as reflections and shadows.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
